### Course API — pre-run health (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Environment: local | Run BEFORE any flow. Stop if any client.test fails.
### Also run: api-test/course/scripts/redis-ping.ps1 → must print PONG

### Boot + MySQL (login endpoint reachable with JSON body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "health-check-nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password",
  "role": "USER"
}

> {%
client.test("Boot reachable: HTTP response with ApiResponse code", function () {
  client.assert(response.status !== 0, "connection failed — is Spring Boot up?");
  client.assert(response.body !== null && response.body.code !== undefined,
      "expected JSON ApiResponse with code");
});
%}

### MinIO live
GET {{minioHealthBase}}/minio/health/live

> {%
client.test("MinIO live 200", function () {
  client.assert(response.status === 200, "MinIO live failed — check tunnel/process on :9000");
});
%}

### MinIO ready
GET {{minioHealthBase}}/minio/health/ready

> {%
client.test("MinIO ready 200", function () {
  client.assert(response.status === 200, "MinIO ready failed");
});
%}
